WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.280
Why did the smartphone go to jail?

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.060
Because it was charged with battery!

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:09.900
Almost all smartphones that we come across

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.160
are rectangular in shape.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:13.400
Why?

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:18.640
Why aren't they shaped in the form of triangles, circles, or maybe squares?

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.500
Let's find out.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:29.620
First, let's talk about the uniqueness of a rectangle.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.400
If we compare the area of a rectangle,

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:37.720
with the areas of a triangle, a circle, or a square of similar dimensions,

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.240
we see that the area of a rectangle is the greatest of all.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.620
So is 'maximum area' the only reason?

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:50.760
Imagine reading text on a circular device.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.980
Do you notice the empty spaces here?

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.060
The area isn't used efficiently.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:00.480
Don't you think the same goes for a triangle as well?

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:05.220
Yes, so we can safely eliminate these two shapes!

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.000
Now, you may argue what's wrong with a square?

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:13.460
We can definitely use its area efficiently, right?

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:17.040
That gets us to an important point.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:18.820
Let's hold both the smartphones,

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.440
in the shape of a square and a rectangle...

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.200
Now we increase the lengths of both the devices

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.140
such that they have the same height.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:29.320
What do you see here?

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:32.160
Don't you think it'll be more difficult to hold this one

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.020
with one hand relative to this one?

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:40.260
Of course! So handling a rectangular device is easier.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.960
Wait, there's more!

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:46.000
While reading the text, we prefer lesser width

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.240
as it's easier on our eyes.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:53.900
And while watching a video, we prefer a wider lens!

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.580
Again the rectangular shape helps us here!

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.340
So, rectangle can be considered as the best shape

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.560
when it comes to smartphones.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:05.120
Great!

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.420
Now for something interesting!

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:11.220
Flip your smartphone and focus on the camera region.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:15.780
If you see carefully, the lens of the camera is circular in shape.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.200
And the images we get on our display

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.860
are rectangular in shape.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.000
What exactly is happening here?

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:28.220
Does the circular lens directly capture rectangular images?

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.980
Or does it capture circular images first

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.460
which are processed into rectangular images?

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.420
What do you think?

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.060
This Kyu Box is open for you to explore.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.100
Do share your thoughts in the comment section below.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.540
And don't forget to subscribe to our channel

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:48.180
to learn about awesome things.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.620
Happy learning!

